WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:04.356
This video shows where SWATrust writes the
output tables of a run,

00:00:04.356 --> 00:00:05.950
and how the files are named.

00:00:06.450 --> 00:00:11.377
The run of this video is the run of Run
streamflow:

00:00:11.377 --> 00:00:17.560
the basin 02070002, 2000 to 2015, with a
warm-up of three years.

00:00:18.062 --> 00:00:19.862
Click Results in the left column.

00:00:20.062 --> 00:00:22.232
In the box Basin, pick the basin.

00:00:23.228 --> 00:00:26.288
Look at Output folders, at the foot of the
left column.

00:00:26.488 --> 00:00:28.338
It has one row for each basin,

00:00:28.338 --> 00:00:32.098
with the name of the basin and the button
Open output folder.

00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:34.270
Click Open output folder.

00:00:37.155 --> 00:00:39.816
The folder out holds one text file for
each

00:00:39.816 --> 00:00:42.725
output table and each step that the run
writes.

00:00:42.925 --> 00:00:44.985
The first part of the name is the table.

00:00:45.185 --> 00:00:46.823
The last part is the step:

00:00:46.823 --> 00:00:50.665
day, mon for month, yr for year, and aa
for the average year.

00:00:51.165 --> 00:00:54.365
Every run has a folder of its own in the
runs folder.

00:00:54.565 --> 00:00:57.755
The name of the folder is the date and the
time of the start.

00:00:58.256 --> 00:01:00.546
The page draws from some of these files.

00:01:00.746 --> 00:01:05.416
It does not show a table as a table: you
open the files with your own programs.

00:01:05.917 --> 00:01:09.987
The next chapter, Read the results, reads
the tables of the water balance.
